hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27536","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Umm Qays bint Mihsan, she said: I entered upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a son of mine who had not yet eaten food, and he urinated on him, so he called for water and sprinkled it over him."
"27537","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Umm Qays bint Mihsan, sister of Ukkashah ibn Mihsan, she said: I entered with a son of mine upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who had not eaten food, and he urinated, so he called for water and sprinkled it. And I entered with a son of mine for whom I had treated throat ailment, and at one time he said: upon him, from udhrah, and said: Why do you torment your children with this pressing? Upon you is this qist - and at one time Sufyan said: Indian oud - for in it are seven cures, among them pleurisy; it is administered through the nose for udhrah and poured in the side of the mouth for pleurisy."
"27538","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sufyan, he said: Thabit Abu al-Miqdam narrated to me, he said: Adi ibn Dinar narrated to me, he said: I heard Umm Qays bint Mihsan say: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the garment stained with menstrual blood. He said: Scrape it with a rib bone, wash it with water, nad, and lote leaves."
"27539","Hajjaj and Hashim narrated to us, they said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Hasan, the freedman of Umm Qays bint Mihsan, from Umm Qays, that she said: My son died and I grieved over him, and I said to the one washing him: Do not wash my son with cold water lest you kill him. Ukkashah ibn Mihsan went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him of her saying. He smiled, then said: What did she say? Long may be her life. He said: I know of no woman who lived as long as she lived."
"27540","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Umm Qays bint Mihsan al-Asadiyyah, sister of Ukkashah, she said: I came with a son of mine for whom I had treated throat ailment, fearing he had udhrah. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Why do you torment your children with these squeezings? Upon you is this Indian oud - meaning kust - for in it are seven cures, among them pleurisy. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took her boy and placed him in his lap, and he urinated on him, so he called for water and sprinkled it, and the boy had not reached eating food. Al-Zuhri said: The sunnah continued that the urine of a boy is sprinkled and the urine of a girl is washed. Al-Zuhri said: It is administered through the nose for udhrah and poured in the mouth side for pleurisy."
"27541","Waki narrated to us, from Israil, from Thabit Abu al-Miqdam, from Adi ibn Dinar, from Umm Qays bint Mihsan, she said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about menstrual blood touching the garment. He said: Scrape it, even with a rib bone."
"27542","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Thabit, from Adi ibn Dinar, the freedman of Umm Qays, from Umm Qays bint Mihsan, she said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about menstrual blood touching the garment. He said: Wash it with water and lote leaves, and scrape it with a rib bone."
"27543","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, that Umm Qays bint Mihsan, one of Banu Asad ibn Khuzaymah, and she was among the first emigrant women who pledged to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: She informed me that she came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a son of hers who had not reached eating food, and he mentioned the hadith, and said: Why do you torment your children?"
"27544","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, and he said: Mamar narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud, from Umm Qays bint Mihsan, that she came with a son of hers for whom she had treated throat ailment from udhrah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: Why do you torment your children with these squeezings? Upon you is this Indian oud, for in it are seven cures, among them pleurisy. Then he took the boy and he urinated on him, so he called for water and sprinkled it. Ibn Shihab said: The sunnah continued with that."
